{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794817866,"nonce":"A/yUxSLJZrrE0Ywhihcy06l+eTQ=","title":"await on a browser-settled future hangs in a threaded hxcpp program","message":"In a threaded Emscripten build (cpp --wasm --threads) main runs on a pthread. Future.await sleeps in slices on that thread, which never yields to the pthread's own event loop. A future settled by the library's threads works (examples/downloads). A future settled by the browser on that same thread never settles: WebGPU's promises (requestAdapter, mapAsync) under emdawnwebgpu, and hxn-gpu-webgl2's completed(), whose fence is polled by emscripten_set_timeout on the thread holding the context.\n\nSeen with temporary probes in both drivers' examples/check, awaiting requestAdapter() and completed() on main's pthread. Both hung, and the same checks without the probe pass.\n\nThe drivers document then rather than await under hxcpp, with or without threads. Under Ash await works, since the GPU sits in a browser agent in a Worker of its own.\n\nWays to make it work:\n- keep the GPU on another thread, an OffscreenCanvas worker of its own, as Ash's browser agent does;\n- have await yield to the event loop while it waits (Asyncify or JSPI);\n- report a clear error when await is called on the thread that has to settle the future.","files":null}]}